# agentpoison_ehragent_attestation_tiering.patch
#
# Parameterize EHRAgent ingest-time attestation tiering for the evaluation sweep.
# Replaces the hardcoded clean-split tier helper (_attestation_tier_for) with
# env-driven, deterministic stratified tiering for BOTH legitimate content and
# injected poison, preserving symmetry (the gate sees only attestation evidence,
# never a poison/legit label):
#   ATTEST_POISON_DISTRIBUTION  (threat profile; e.g. "N:1.0" | "W:1.0" | "S:1.0")
#   ATTEST_LEGIT_DISTRIBUTION   (deployment regime; e.g. "N:0.80,W:0.15,S:0.05")
# Defaults ("N:1.0" poison / "S:1.0" legit) reproduce the verified clean-split
# baseline byte-for-byte (ASR-r 100 gate-off, 0 gate-on).
#
# Base: branch feature/attestation-retrieval, medagent.py with hardcoded
#       _attestation_tier_for helper.
# Apply from the AgentPoison repo root:
#   git apply patches/agentpoison_ehragent_attestation_tiering.patch
#
--- a/EhrAgent/ehragent/medagent.py	2026-06-28 06:24:56.408999689 +0000
+++ b/EhrAgent/ehragent/medagent.py	2026-06-28 06:24:56.688600882 +0000
